I still cannot believe
that we get to launch

00:24:45.025 --> 00:24:48.129
our second season from Hollywood.

00:24:48.129 --> 00:24:50.501
(audience cheering)

00:24:50.501 --> 00:24:55.210
To make the most of this
moment right now and honor it

00:24:55.210 --> 00:24:56.850
in a way it truly deserves.

00:24:56.850 --> 00:24:58.749
I wanted to take a look back

00:24:58.749 --> 00:25:01.740
at some of the places that shaped me

00:25:01.740 --> 00:25:03.880
and I wanted to take you with me.

00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:06.823
This is an intimate tour of my LA.

00:25:08.561 --> 00:25:13.561
I'm gonna take us to
the first place I lived

00:25:14.610 --> 00:25:16.753
until I was seven years old.

00:25:19.170 --> 00:25:20.283
Hang on to your hat.

00:25:22.813 --> 00:25:26.321
They've really made it
look so much more romantic.

00:25:26.321 --> 00:25:28.690
The bars were on the windows

00:25:28.690 --> 00:25:30.733
because it just wasn't safe enough,

00:25:30.733 --> 00:25:33.294
but the neighborhood's
gotten so much better.

00:25:33.294 --> 00:25:36.833
God I'm so tempted to just
beg them to let me in.

00:25:37.813 --> 00:25:40.396
(gentle music)

00:25:46.789 --> 00:25:51.053
I don't have to be lonely anymore.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.993
I was so lonely in this house.

00:25:54.876 --> 00:25:56.650
It was just me and my mom.

00:25:56.650 --> 00:26:01.220
And it was just a really sad energy.

00:26:01.220 --> 00:26:03.403
It was very empty and very lonely.

00:26:04.281 --> 00:26:09.281
And I grew up and got in
charge of my own destiny.

00:26:09.780 --> 00:26:12.469
And now my house is like
Grand Central Station.

00:26:12.469 --> 00:26:17.200
There's so much life and
there's so many people

00:26:18.920 --> 00:26:21.320
and this place just taught me

00:26:21.320 --> 00:26:24.990
that I wasn't the kind of
person who wanted to live

00:26:24.990 --> 00:26:29.990
in a quiet, lonely place.

00:26:30.590 --> 00:26:34.847
I wanted to live a life where
I was around a lot of people.

00:26:34.847 --> 00:26:37.430
(upbeat music)

00:26:38.360 --> 00:26:43.360
I learned to drive at Sophia
Loren's ranch in Calabasas.

00:26:44.013 --> 00:26:47.260
Her two sons, Carlo and Edoardo taught me

00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:49.270
in a Renault Le car.

00:26:49.270 --> 00:26:51.070
And they taught me on a stick shift.

00:26:53.763 --> 00:26:57.340
Oh my god, when I was trying
to attempt sleeping at night,

00:26:57.340 --> 00:27:00.773
even though I was just so scared,

00:27:00.773 --> 00:27:05.120
this is what cats sound
like when they are mating.

00:27:05.120 --> 00:27:05.953
Are you ready?

00:27:07.313 --> 00:27:11.313
(Drew making cat mating sounds)

00:27:13.133 --> 00:27:15.993
That was the soundtrack to this apartment.

00:27:17.841 --> 00:27:20.730
As much as the building looks charming,

00:27:20.730 --> 00:27:22.720
back in the 70s,

00:27:22.720 --> 00:27:26.273
there was a lot of like, don't
park your car at night alone.

00:27:26.273 --> 00:27:27.870
There's bars on the windows.

00:27:27.870 --> 00:27:29.469
There's bars on the individual apartments.

00:27:29.469 --> 00:27:33.190
I mean, for a 14 year old, I was scared

00:27:34.330 --> 00:27:39.260
and I'm not scared anymore.

00:27:39.260 --> 00:27:42.593
I'm not scared anymore at all.

00:27:45.410 --> 00:27:50.410
I definitely am glad that
my kids, no matter what,

00:27:50.890 --> 00:27:53.630
cause we're gonna, all of
us are gonna screw it up

00:27:53.630 --> 00:27:55.510
with our kids, we're gonna do our best,

00:27:55.510 --> 00:27:57.740
but we're gonna make mistakes.

00:27:57.740 --> 00:28:01.630
I'm so glad that my kids
won't be having to live

00:28:01.630 --> 00:28:03.213
on their own at 14.

00:28:04.181 --> 00:28:09.181
And that's as healing to the
14 year old me as it can get.

00:28:13.822 --> 00:28:15.072
Oh, this is it.

00:28:16.867 --> 00:28:19.730
Oh my god, it's still here.

00:28:19.730 --> 00:28:21.113
The Washing Machine.

00:28:23.981 --> 00:28:26.160
This is such a dream to be here.

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:27.590
I spent years here.

00:28:27.590 --> 00:28:31.830
When I first lived in my
apartment that I was so scared in,

00:28:31.830 --> 00:28:36.310
the truth was is that I would
let the laundry and dishes

00:28:36.310 --> 00:28:37.240
and everything pile up.

00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:39.200
I didn't know how to clean,

00:28:39.200 --> 00:28:43.845
but this was where I learned
how to take care of myself.

00:28:43.845 --> 00:28:48.510
The books were the school and
this was the domestic journey

00:28:48.510 --> 00:28:51.689
of learning how to live on your own.

00:28:51.689 --> 00:28:54.510
Kids don't know how to
take care of themselves

00:28:54.510 --> 00:28:55.823
until you teach them.

00:28:57.350 --> 00:29:00.029
Olive and Frankie, I'm coming for you.

00:29:00.029 --> 00:29:02.612
(upbeat music)

00:29:08.625 --> 00:29:10.100
(audience cheering)

00:29:10.100 --> 00:29:13.700
That was the start of
my stain removal story.

00:29:13.700 --> 00:29:15.690
You know we have a segment on our show

00:29:15.690 --> 00:29:18.030
called Stan for Stains,

00:29:18.030 --> 00:29:22.390
and I absolutely just
loved taking this tour

00:29:22.390 --> 00:29:23.610
and sharing it with you.

00:29:23.610 --> 00:29:24.933
That's why I did it,

00:29:24.933 --> 00:29:28.890
including our last stop it's
a place I haven't been back to

00:29:28.890 --> 00:29:30.240
in a long time.

00:29:30.240 --> 00:29:33.060
It's the institution where
I spent a year and a half

00:29:33.060 --> 00:29:36.853
of my life and take a look.

00:29:37.997 --> 00:29:40.780
(upbeat music)

00:29:40.780 --> 00:29:41.683
It's right here.

00:29:42.790 --> 00:29:44.550
- [Lady] The place with
all the barbed wire?

00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:45.703
- Yeah that's it.

00:29:48.510 --> 00:29:53.510
I was a real wild child and
I just got so out of control

00:29:54.070 --> 00:29:57.753
that no one knew what to do with me.

00:29:58.930 --> 00:30:02.160
And so my mom called a friend

00:30:02.160 --> 00:30:04.160
because her daughter was out of control

00:30:04.160 --> 00:30:08.480
and they drove me here in
the middle of the night

00:30:08.480 --> 00:30:10.891
and they walked me right
through those two doors.

00:30:10.891 --> 00:30:13.940
And when you go through those two doors,

00:30:13.940 --> 00:30:15.313
you do not come out.

00:30:16.640 --> 00:30:19.263
And I was there for a year and a half.

00:30:20.600 --> 00:30:24.860
I think this is important
for me to share with people

00:30:24.860 --> 00:30:27.000
because when they watch our show,

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:28.680
we have a very beautiful set

00:30:29.980 --> 00:30:34.420
and I get to dress in nice clothing

00:30:34.420 --> 00:30:37.210
and get my hair and makeup done.

00:30:37.210 --> 00:30:40.793
And there's an elegance
hopefully to the show,

00:30:41.985 --> 00:30:46.409
but I will never lose sight
of this part of my story.

00:30:46.409 --> 00:30:50.609
And I have seen and been through things

00:30:50.609 --> 00:30:55.609
and they've helped me just
recognize in all of us

00:30:58.490 --> 00:31:02.900
that we go through steps and
it can't be embarrassing.

00:31:02.900 --> 00:31:04.693
It has to be our strengths.

00:31:05.580 --> 00:31:07.910
It has to be something
that we can be proud of

00:31:07.910 --> 00:31:10.330
because we overcame it and we look back

00:31:10.330 --> 00:31:13.843
with honor and humor.

00:31:16.430 --> 00:31:21.380
Life is so wonderful compared
to what it was in this place.

00:31:21.380 --> 00:31:26.380
I can't even believe I actually
get to be where I am now.

00:31:27.050 --> 00:31:29.660
Cause when I was here, I didn't see that,

00:31:29.660 --> 00:31:31.390
I thought I would be here forever.

00:31:31.390 --> 00:31:35.067
I never thought I was gonna
make it to somewhere better.

00:31:35.067 --> 00:31:39.673
And I'm just so happy with my life.

00:31:39.673 --> 00:31:43.010
And I don't know if I
would have the life I have

00:31:43.010 --> 00:31:46.220
if it wasn't for a place like this.

00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:47.053
So

00:31:49.907 --> 00:31:52.482
it was so important to come here today,

00:31:52.482 --> 00:31:56.840
just honor this.

00:31:56.840 --> 00:31:58.456
It's very empowering.

00:31:58.456 --> 00:32:01.400
It's very celebratory.

00:32:01.400 --> 00:32:04.530
I just get to visit it in
my dreams and wave hello

00:32:04.530 --> 00:32:06.513
and know I'm not here anymore.

00:32:07.429 --> 00:32:08.703
That's pretty cool.

